    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.ai\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI need two escape to back to normal mod, for example, I type ci'esc', it is still in operator pending mode, and I type 'esc>'again I can back to normal mod, which just need a single esc to back to normal if  I disable this plugin.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.10\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\ntype ci'esc'\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nback to normal mod\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\ntwo escape to back normal",
